      "#### Key words",
      "",
      "> **Sentence —** a group of words expressing a complete thought.",
      ">",
      "> **Subject —** the part of a sentence naming who or what it is about.",
      ">",
      "> **Predicate —** the part of a sentence saying something about the subject.",
      ">",
      "> **Simple subject —** the head noun or pronoun of the subject.",
      ">",
      "> **Complete subject —** the head noun with everything attached to it.",
      ">",
      "> **Clause —** a group of words containing a subject and a verb.",
      ">",
      "> **Phrase —** a group of words without both a subject and a verb.",
      ">",
      "> **Independent clause —** a clause that can stand alone as a sentence.",
      ">",
      "> **Dependent clause —** a clause that cannot stand alone.",
      ">",
      "> **Subordinate clause —** another name for a dependent clause.",
      ">",
      "> **Simple sentence —** one independent clause.",
      ">",
      "> **Compound sentence —** two or more independent clauses joined.",
      ">",
      "> **Complex sentence —** one independent clause with at least one dependent clause.",
      "",
      "",
      "",
      "> **Comma splice —** the error of joining two independent clauses with only a comma.",
      ">",
      "> **Fragment —** a group of words punctuated as a sentence but not complete.",
