      "",
      "- Advice is given well when it is hedged, leaving the other person free to refuse it.",
      "",
      "- A disagreement that keeps a conversation going has three parts: a concession, the disagreement, and a reason.",
      "",
      "- Softening the manner is good practice; softening the point is not.",
      "",
      "- Everyday functions — requesting, refusing, apologising, thanking, interrupting — each have their own set expressions.",
      "",
      "- Four context clues let you estimate an unfamiliar word: definition, contrast, example and general sense.",
