      "#### Key words",
      "",
      "> **Proverb —** a short well-known saying stating a general truth or piece of advice.",
      ">",
      "> **Literal meaning —** what the words say on the surface.",
      ">",
      "> **Figurative meaning —** what the words are really being used to say.",
      ">",
      "> **Imagery —** the picture a saying puts into the mind.",
      ">",
      "> **Idiom —** an expression whose meaning cannot be worked out from its words.",
      ">",
      "> **Aesthetic language —** language chosen for its beauty and force as well as its sense.",
      ">",
      "> **Wisdom literature —** the body of sayings a community passes on.",
      ">",
      "> **Equivalent —** a saying in another language carrying the same sense.",
      ">",
      "> **Context —** the situation in which something is said.",
      ">",
      "> **Register —** the level of formality; proverbs vary in this too.",
      ">",
      "> **Oral tradition —** knowledge passed on by speech rather than writing.",
