      "",
      "decoration. It is a compressed argument that a whole community has already agreed with, and using one well puts that agreement behind you.",
      "",
      "#### 11.1 What a proverb is",
      "",
      "A **proverb** is a short, well-known saying that states a general truth or gives advice. Three things are true of nearly all of them.",
      "",
      "**They are short.** A proverb that has to be explained at length has failed.",
      "",
      "- **They speak in pictures.** Almost every proverb says one thing in order to mean another.",
      "",
      "- **They are common property.** Nobody owns a proverb; a speaker who uses one is quoting a whole",
      "",
      "- community.",
      "",
      "This is why every proverb has two meanings at once. The **literal meaning** is what the words say on the surface. The **figurative meaning** is what they are being used to say. A listener who takes a proverb literally has missed the point entirely.",
      "",
      "| **Proverb** | **Literal meaning** | **Figurative meaning** |",
