      "",
      "> **Common misconception 11.2**",
      ">",
      "> A pair of proverbs is rarely an exact match. *A single hand cannot lift the roof* and *many hands make light work* overlap, but the first says the task is impossible alone while the second says it is merely easier together. When you match a pair, be ready to say where they differ as well as where they agree.",
      "",
      "#### 11.4 Using a proverb in a sentence of your own",
      "",
      "A proverb is quoted, not paraphrased. It goes into your writing whole, and it is usually introduced by a short phrase that shows you know you are quoting.",
      "",
      "| **Way of introducing it** | **Example** |",
