      "#### 13.1 Personal narrative",
      "",
      "A **personal narrative** tells something that happened to you. It is written in the **first person**, using *I* and *we*, and its whole business is to make a reader feel they were there.",
      "",
      "##### 13.1.1 Planning before you write",
      "",
      "| **Decide** | **Ask yourself** |",
      "| --- | --- |",
      "| The event | What single thing am I telling? Not the whole day — one event. |",
      "| The point | Why is it worth telling? What did it change or reveal? |",
      "| The setting | Where and when? What could be seen, heard and smelt there? |",
      "| The sequence | What happened first, next, last? Where does it begin and end? |",
      "| The feeling | What did I feel then, and what do I feel now looking back? |",
