      "#### Engage",
      "",
      "Long before anybody in this country wrote a book, the stories were all here. They were told at night, in courtyards, by people who had learnt them from people who had learnt them from people. Ananse was already old. The dirges were already being sung. Literature is not something that arrived with printing; printing merely gave it a second home. This chapter looks at both homes — the one on the page and the older one in the mouth.",
